(7217170, 1112079, 138253, '<td valign="top">my 2nd highest vote in the challenge with a 9<br/>the title is an adage i have not heard in a long time and is a fresh take on shooting such a (pardon the obvious pun) powder keg of a subject.<br/>i''ve upvoted imagery here that has gone against the standard of just taking pictures of firearms and have thrown a new perspective at people to see a different idea of "gun".<br/>time''s arrow points us ever forward, with no offramp to go back and see what was missed, and is met at the end with a sudden and inevitable stop.</td>', 'my 2nd highest vote in the challenge with a 9the title is an adage i have not heard in a long time and is a fresh take on shooting such a (pardon the obvious pun) powder keg of a subject.i''ve upvoted imagery here that has gone against the standard of just taking pictures of firearms and have thrown a new perspective at people to see a different idea of "gun".time''s arrow points us ever forward, with no offramp to go back and see what was missed, and is met at the end with a sudden and inevitable stop.', '2014-05-15 16:47:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(7217172, 1112375, 138253, '<td valign="top">one of my top scores given out (a 9).<br/>Kudos for changing the perspective to the flower in the challenge of guns.<br/>Many may read my comments on this challenge (and my scores moreso) as a general "anti gun person" - which is not the case. I think they have a time and place, and I love the minimal amount of gun here, showcasing that peace can grow out of the fading of arming ourselves.<br/>that is not always the case, i''m not naieve, but anybody who believes the opposite is blind to a cyclical arms race that will inevitably come about from wide-spread like-minded mentality.</td>', 'one of my top scores given out (a 9).Kudos for changing the perspective to the flower in the challenge of guns.Many may read my comments on this challenge (and my scores moreso) as a general "anti gun person" - which is not the case. I think they have a time and place, and I love the minimal amount of gun here, showcasing that peace can grow out of the fading of arming ourselves.that is not always the case, i''m not naieve, but anybody who believes the opposite is blind to a cyclical arms race that will inevitably come about from wide-spread like-minded mentality.', '2014-05-15 16:51:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(7217173, 1112591, 138253, '<td valign="top">this made me laugh. i don''t know why, but after seeing shot after shot of things that shoot, and then seeing THIS.<br/> <br/>Bravo Sir! (or madam).<br/>you''re getting a 9 from me.</td>', 'this made me laugh. i don''t know why, but after seeing shot after shot of things that shoot, and then seeing THIS. Bravo Sir! (or madam).you''re getting a 9 from me.', '2014-05-15 16:51:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(7217175, 1112382, 138253, '<td valign="top">i commented on my other 9 vote given to a gun/flower image my thoughts about the idea of peace coming out of the disarming of ourselves and think that it is equally true in this image, and can be easily transitioned to applying that mentality to "how we arm our children to deal with the world".<br/>teaching our youth that guns are the key will not promote peace, but teaching our children the right and wrong times to arm one-self (with whatever weapon) is one of the most important things a parent can do.<br/> <br/>there is a lot of symbolism that can be taken from this image (water to give life to plants, peace coming from disarming, no peace without protection, peace prospering out of the remnants of war....there are many many more) and I hope that is not lost on people (not just voters here, but on our species as a collective whole, because if it is, we won''t be around for much longer.<br/> <br/>/rant</td>', 'i commented on my other 9 vote given to a gun/flower image my thoughts about the idea of peace coming out of the disarming of ourselves and think that it is equally true in this image, and can be easily transitioned to applying that mentality to "how we arm our children to deal with the world".teaching our youth that guns are the key will not promote peace, but teaching our children the right and wrong times to arm one-self (with whatever weapon) is one of the most important things a parent can do. there is a lot of symbolism that can be taken from this image (water to give life to plants, peace coming from disarming, no peace without protection, peace prospering out of the remnants of war....there are many many more) and I hope that is not lost on people (not just voters here, but on our species as a collective whole, because if it is, we won''t be around for much longer. /rant', '2014-05-15 16:56:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(7217368, 1112582, 174999, '<td valign="top">Hippie days... I really like composition of this photo being surrounded in flowers..its different.<br/> <br/> I would have liked to seen the gun sight on the center of that flower giving it a more impact. Same level of where the gun is, just more centered.<br/> I actually had to up the vote too from what I had. Nice job :-))</td>', 'Hippie days... I really like composition of this photo being surrounded in flowers..its different.  I would have liked to seen the gun sight on the center of that flower giving it a more impact. Same level of where the gun is, just more centered. I actually had to up the vote too from what I had. Nice job :-))', '2014-05-16 06:49:38.000000', NULL, 1),
